# lists

there are lists that let you change the keyboard size, layout, and physical standard.

## size list

<!-- NOTE: add gif here -->

press `s` to open the size list. this determines which physical key matrix ditto renders.

| size | form factor |
| --- | --- |
| `60%` | compact, no f-row or arrows |
| `65%` | 60% with arrow keys and a navigation cluster |
| `75%` | f-row in a compact layout |
| `80%` | tenkeyless, with an f-row and arrows but no numpad |
| `96%` | compact full-size layout with a numpad |
| `100%` | full-size layout |

## layout list

<!-- NOTE: add gif here -->

press `l` to open the layout list. this determines how physical keys are remapped.

| layout | description |
| --- | --- |
| `qwerty` | standard us layout |
| `qwerty uk` | standard uk layout |
| `qwertz` | german qwertz layout |
| `dvorak` | dvorak simplified layout |
| `dvorak uk` | dvorak uk layout |
| `colemak` | colemak layout |
| `colemak-dh` | colemak with the angle mod |
| `workman` | workman layout |
| `azerty` | french azerty layout |

[custom layouts](/custom-layouts) also appear in this list after ditto loads them at startup.

## standard list

<!-- NOTE: add gif here -->

press `d` to open the standard list. this determines the physical keyboard standard.

| standard | description |
| --- | --- |
| `ansi` | american national standards institute |
| `iso` | international organization for standardization |
| `abnt` | brazilian technical standards association |
| `jis` | japanese industrial standard |
| `ks` | korean standard |

press `c` to toggle the kana overlay for jis or the hangeul overlay for ks.

